\label{sec: syn_exp}
Following \citet{pedregosa2016hyperparameter, grazzi2020iteration, chen2022decentralized}, $f_i$ and $g_i$ are defined as:

\begin{align*}
    &f_i(\lambda, \omega) = \sum_{(x_e,y_e)\in\mathcal{D}_i'}\psi(y_ex_e^{\top}\omega), \\
    &g_i(\lambda, \omega) = \sum_{(x_e,y_e)\in\mathcal{D}_i}\psi(y_ex_e^{\top}\omega) + \frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{p}e^{\lambda_i}\omega_i^2,
\end{align*}
where $\psi(x) = \log(1 + e^{-x})$ and $p=200$ denotes the dimension parameter.

 The filtration is defined as
    \[
        \mathcal{F}_k = \sigma\left(\bigcup_{i=1}^{n}\{y_{i,0}^{(T)}, ..., y_{i,k}^{(T)}, x_{i,0},...,x_{i,k}, r_{i,0},...,r_{i,k}\} \right).
    \]
